# ═══ Draft knowledge entry — autotools cross mode "assumed OK" optional-dep
# probes silently enable targets whose headers are absent
# Software: libtheora 1.2.0-alpha1
# Gate: conan-verify G2 (conan create, ohos-aarch64)
# Status: DRAFT

id: libtheora-1.2.0-alpha1-cross-mode-assumed-optional-deps
severity: 2
category: build-system|configure|ohos
trigger_tool: configure|make
phase: configure|compilation

keywords: cross compiling; assumed OK, XIPH_PATH_VORBIS, optional dependency, examples, --host, --build, native mode, config.guess
error_signature: cross compiling; assumed OK|fatal error: '[a-z0-9]+/[a-z_]+\.h' file not found.*examples/
match_keywords: cross compiling, assumed OK, XIPH_PATH_VORBIS, vorbis/codec.h, encoder_example, optional dependency, noinst, examples, --host, --build, dual triplet, native mode, config.guess

root_cause: |
  Forcing configure into cross mode with --host=aarch64-linux-ohos
  --build=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu (the sdl-image/aalib convention for
  bypassing HMDFS conftest issues) has a side effect on upstream macros that
  PROBE optional dependencies with run tests: in cross mode they cannot run
  the probe, so they "assume OK". libtheora 1.2.0alpha1's XIPH_PATH_VORBIS
  prints "checking for Vorbis... cross compiling; assumed OK..." and enables
  the vorbis-dependent noinst example programs (encoder_example.c includes
  <vorbis/codec.h>). The build then fails with "vorbis/codec.h file not
  found" even though libvorbis is intentionally not a dependency of the
  package.

rec_approach: native-mode-with-vendored-modern-config-scripts
rec_description: |
  When the upstream tarball's bundled config.guess/config.sub is the only
  reason for cross mode, prefer NATIVE mode and vendor a modern,
  HarmonyOS-patched pair instead (repo precedent: babeltrace2 2.1.2
  patches/autotools/config/, GNU config 2023-08-22 base — the 2010-era
  libtheora pair is from 2003 and even patch-autotools-ohos.pl cannot match
  its patterns). In native mode the vorbis pkg-config probe fails cleanly,
  the optional examples are skipped (upstream behaviour for missing optional
  deps), and the core libraries build untrimmed. Combine with the E011
  umask/mktemp in-source patch so config.status survives HMDFS, plus the
  shared-dep LD_LIBRARY_PATH injection if a shared conan dependency is
  linked into conftests (see companion draft
  libtheora-1.2.0-alpha1-shared-dep-conftest-runtime-path).

  Rule of thumb: dual-triplet cross mode is for "cannot run conftests at
  all"; native mode is required when upstream macros make cross-mode
  ASSUMPTIONS about optional dependencies that the environment cannot
  honour.

rec_commands:
  - "bash config.guess  # expect aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos with the vendored pair"
  - "conan create archives/l/libtheora/1.2.0-alpha1 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing"

verification: |
  libtheora 1.2.0-alpha1: cross mode fails in examples/ (vorbis/codec.h);
  native mode with vendored 2023 config.guess/config.sub + E011 umask patch
  configures cleanly ("no optimization for your platform" asm note is
  expected on aarch64), builds all three libraries and passes 9/9 upstream
  tests plus the consumer roundtrip test_package.

related:
  - knowledge/drafts/sdl-image-1.2.12-autotools-cross-ohos.kv (dual-triplet convention — counter-case where cross mode is right)
  - knowledge/graph/E007.kv (config.guess/config.sub HarmonyOS patching)
  - archives/l/libtheora/1.2.0-alpha1/conanfile.py (NOTE comment in generate())
last_updated: 2026-09-18
